    <statement><p>For the following indefinite integral, find the full power series centered at <m>x=0</m> and then give the first 5 nonzero terms of the power series and the open interval of convergence.</p>
<p><me>f(x) = \int \frac{\ln(1+x)}{x}\ dx</me></p>
<p><m>f(x) = C + \displaystyle\sum\limits_{n=1}^{\infty}</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><m>f(x) = C +</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0002"/> <m>+</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0003"/> <m>+</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0004"/> <m>+</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0005"/> <m>+</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0006"/> <m>+ \cdots</m></p>
<p>The open interval of convergence is: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0007"/> (Give your answer in .)</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{\left(-1\right)^{n+1}x^{-1+n+1}}{n\mathopen{}\left(-1+n+1\right)}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{x^{-1+2}}{1\cdot \left(-1+2\right)}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{-1x^{-1+3}}{2\cdot \left(-1+3\right)}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{x^{-1+4}}{3\cdot \left(-1+4\right)}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{-1x^{-1+5}}{4\cdot \left(-1+5\right)}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{x^{-1+6}}{5\cdot \left(-1+6\right)}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left(-1,1\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
